      },
      "model_overhangs_review": "All 22 labelled islands are assigned below; there are no model-rooted or unlabelled bodies. The display storey beside the opening is solid down to the lintel and each display catch opens plumb into the bay, so the front bay tree carries the lintel, the front housing strip's hidden underside and both catches from the bed. The top band's height range makes this slice plan the tree support on its own layer grid: 572 support-only layers of up to 0.28 mm between the 0.24 object layers, and 274.5 g of support where v7 printed 192.9 g on the object layers. On that grid the housing strip (17) and both catches (19, 20) read as interface islands where v7's same front body reached them unlabelled; v7's centre body (west backing roof, west inner well, keystone roof) is part of the west body here, which also takes the centre backing roof and the east inner well roof from v7's east body. Cleanup precedes every hardware installation and the shell join; actual effort and finish are unmeasured.",
