          "contact_region": "West and centre bed-rooted branch system: west fixed spring cup (interfaces 1, 3), west and centre carrier backing roofs (5, 6), west service-slot and handhold-recess roofs (8, 10), west outer, west inner and east inner hardware-well roofs (12, 13, 14), the pump-jack receptacle pocket roof (18) and the west funnel-brim surround (21).",
          "removal_lane": "With the shell loose and all hardware absent, detach individual interface branches at their exposed stems. Pull fixed-cup bore branches aft (+Y) out of the cup mouths into the service recess; release cup underside branches downward. Lower the common backing/well roof branches into their open cavities and remove aft through the open enclosure. The outer channel branches leave through the side service opening; the higher inner-recess branches first lower into that opening. Clean the keystone pocket through its open fore/aft aperture before the jack is fitted. Funnel-bearing branches detach toward X0 into the open funnel mouth and leave through that opening. This is branch-by-branch removal; no intact-tree rigid translation is asserted.",
          "removal_direction_original_cad": "Cup bores +Y; mechanism roof branches \u2212Z then +Y or outboard \u2212X through the service opening; keystone roof through its aperture along Y; funnel branches toward X0 then through its open mouth.",
